\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces The hierarchical predictor architecture for exotoxin classification. The model employs a two-step approach to address class imbalance and improve classification accuracy. In the first stage, a high-level classifier groups exotoxins into broader type families based on their prevalence in the dataset. In \textcolor {red}{\textst  {the}}~\textcolor {blue}{a} second stage, a specialized classifier is applied within each group to refine the classification and distinguish specific exotoxin types that share similar features.}}{18}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hier_logic}{{3.2}{18}{The hierarchical predictor architecture for exotoxin classification. The model employs a two-step approach to address class imbalance and improve classification accuracy. In the first stage, a high-level classifier groups exotoxins into broader type families based on their prevalence in the dataset. In \replace {the}{a} second stage, a specialized classifier is applied within each group to refine the classification and distinguish specific exotoxin types that share similar features}{figure.caption.8}{}}
