\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces \small  Descriptive analysis of bacterial exotoxin feature: sequence length. (a) Sequence length distribution for different bacterial exotoxin types, measured in amino acids. The x-axis exhibit the exotoxin types, with each Type described by a colour: Type I (blue), Type II (orange), Type III (pink), Type IV (green), and Unknown (yellow). The y-axis shows sequence length in amino acids, ranging from 0 to approximately 3000, excluding three outliers. (b) Sequence length distribution for bacterial exotoxin targets, measured in amino acids. The x-axis represents the exotoxin targets, with each category represented by a distinct colour: Vertebrates (dark green) and Non-vertebrates (purple). The y-axis shows sequence length in amino acids, ranging from 0 to approximately 2500, excluding five outliers.}}{23}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
